<title>BRAZIL: Sept sees record Brazil petroleum use - Petrobras.</title>
<headline>Sept sees record Brazil petroleum use - Petrobras.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Consumption in Brazil of petroleum products averaged a record 1,649,300 barrels per day (bpd) in September, up 5.3 percent from August,state-run energy monopoly Petrobras said in a statement.</p>
<p>The figure also represents a 9.7 percent increase on the same month last year, it added.</p>
<p>Of the total, diesel accounted for 587,900 barrels bpd and gasoline 291,800 bpd, it said.</p>
<p>-- Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151</p>
</text>
